  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is implicated in a complex network of interactions that ultimately lead to the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6. The evidence suggests that Phellandral, (R)- acts as a target for Cornuside, which in turn targets the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6. This indicates a chain of enzymatic interactions where Phellandral, (R)- is indirectly linked to the target enzyme through Cornuside. Additionally, Phellandral, (R)- is also shown to target UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B15, which is further linked to the same target enzyme. This suggests that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its effects through multiple pathways, with the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6 being a downstream target in both direct and indirect pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Phellandral, (R)- to influence the enzyme through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving metabolic or signaling pathways that are not fully elucidated.",
